OL,3,GNEWSA'Improvise, adapt and overcome',
OL,4,Asays veteran who lost both legs in IED
OL,5,Ablast
OL,6,
OL,7,FA former soldier who lost both his legs
OL,8,Fwhen he stepped on an improvised
OL,9,Fexplosive device (IED) in Afghanistan
OL,10,F16 years ago said he wanted to show
OL,11,Fother people with disabilities what you
OL,12,Fcan achieve with a bit of willpower and
OL,13,Fpreparation.
OL,15,FRick Clement, who served with 1st
OL,16,FBattalion The Duke of Lancaster's
OL,17,FRegiment, only learned of his
OL,18,Flife-changing injuries when he woke up
OL,19,Fin hospital three weeks after the blast
OL,20,Fin May 2010.
OL,23,APub: 10-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
